<BaseLayout title="Portfolio counting decisions | FTFN">
  <section class="page-section prose-page">
    <h1 class="page-title">Portfolio identity and counting decisions</h1>
    <p class="lede">The 103 determinations from {decisions.decision_date} are retained below. {namedDossierAdditions.length} dated additions from Nevada, Europe, Southern Africa, South Asia, Chile, Brazil, the North Sea, Stockholm, Auckland, Singapore West, Busan, Hamburg, Madrid, Mexico City, Copenhagen, Helsinki, Switzerland, Kenya, Gauteng, Malaysia, Colombia, Morocco, Portugal, Italy and Austria have been reviewed under the same owner-authorized AI policy. Latest review: {current.current_review_date}; each group retains its own date.</p>
    <p>{authorized.portfolio.policy}</p>
    <p>Named programs may count once when their child facilities or projects are not also counted. National and supranational orientations do not count as localized place dossiers. A clearly labelled subnational region, corridor, locality, campus or basin can qualify without pretending to be a municipality.</p>
    <p>The retained inventory has {current.historical_projects} project identities and {current.historical_places} place identities. The November additions contribute {current.added_projects} projects and {current.added_places} places.</p>
    <table data-current-portfolio><caption>Current eligible identities, not completed-dossier totals</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Scope</th><th scope="col">Eligible identities</th><th scope="col">Target</th><th scope="col">More needed</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">Projects</th><td>{current.eligible_projects}</td><td>100</td><td>{current.projects_needed}</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Places</th><td>{current.eligible_places}</td><td>70</td><td>{current.places_needed}</td></tr></tbody></table>
    <p>{current.boundary}</p>
    <p>{dossiers.records.length} Montana proposal-stage dossiers have now been authored and AI-reviewed, completing this 32-project cohort. Other eligible identities still need content completion or exact-version AI review; none is waiting for a human signature. This is not completion of the full portfolio target. Operating outcomes require their own evidence.</p>
    <p>{localities.records.length} localized place accounts are also complete as dated, bounded readings. Their identities were already included in the 25 eligible-place inventory, so no new places are added to that count. <a href="/atlas/places/">Read the locality accounts</a>.</p>
    <p><a href="/atlas/projects/montana-bead/">Read the complete Montana cohort</a> · <a href="/data/build-decisions.json">Download all decisions and dossier inputs</a></p>
  </section>
  <section class="page-section"><h2>Nevada additions reviewed {nevadaDossiers.inspected_date}</h2><p>Two separate project articles replace no historical input. The comparative parent contributes zero projects. The county is a separately defined receiving system within a wider corridor, not an independent impact observation to add to that corridor's results.</p>{nevadaDossiers.records.map(r=><details data-portfolio-addition={r.record_id}><summary>{r.title}</summary><p><a href={r.route}>{r.scope}</a></p><p>{r.identity_decision.rationale}</p><p>Eligible count: {r.identity_decision.eligible_count}. Dated article authored and AI self-reviewed; production verification pending.</p></details>)}</section>
  <section class="page-section"><h2>European additions reviewed {europeDossiers.inspected_date}</h2><p>Hinkley Point C counts once as a two-unit project; Olkiluoto 3 counts as one unit without counting its site again. Somerset uses the exact unitary-authority area, not the ceremonial county.</p>{europeDossiers.records.map(r=><details data-portfolio-addition={r.record_id}><summary>{r.title}</summary><p><a href={r.route}>{r.scope}</a></p><p>{r.identity_decision.rationale}</p><p>Eligible count: {r.identity_decision.eligible_count}. Dated article authored and AI self-reviewed; production verification pending.</p></details>)}</section>
  <section class="page-section"><h2>Southern African additions reviewed {southernAfricaDossiers.inspected_date}</h2><p>Lesotho Highlands Phase II counts once without counting its component contracts again. Mokhotlong District and Cape Town municipality retain their administrative scopes, distinct from project footprints and supply systems.</p>{southernAfricaDossiers.records.map(r=><details data-portfolio-addition={r.record_id}><summary>{r.title}</summary><p><a href={r.route}>{r.scope}</a></p><p>{r.identity_decision.rationale}</p><p>Eligible count: {r.identity_decision.eligible_count}. Dated article authored and AI self-reviewed; production verification pending.</p></details>)}</section>
  <section class="page-section"><h2>South Asian additions reviewed {southAsiaDossiers.inspected_date}</h2><p>Mumbai Line 3 and Dhaka Line 6 each count once across construction and financing stages. Greater Mumbai is one municipal place, not the entire metropolitan region.</p>{southAsiaDossiers.records.map(r=><details data-portfolio-addition={r.record_id}><summary>{r.title}</summary><p><a href={r.route}>{r.scope}</a></p><p>{r.identity_decision.rationale}</p><p>Eligible count: {r.identity_decision.eligible_count}. Dated article authored and AI self-reviewed; production verification pending.</p></details>)}</section>
  <section class="page-section"><h2>Chile additions reviewed {chileDossiers.inspected_date}</h2><p>Cerro Pabellón and Atacama drinking-water desalination are separate projects. Copiapó municipality is a receiving place, not the whole province or the desalination service area.</p>{chileDossiers.records.map(r=><details data-portfolio-addition={r.record_id}><summary>{r.title}</summary><p><a href={r.route}>{r.scope}</a></p><p>{r.identity_decision.rationale}</p><p><a href={r.historical_acquisition.route}>Retained acquisition record</a>. {r.historical_acquisition.decision}.</p><p>Eligible count: {r.identity_decision.eligible_count}. Dated article authored and AI self-reviewed; production verification pending.</p></details>)}</section>
  <section class="page-section"><h2>Brazil additions reviewed {brazilDossiers.inspected_date}</h2><p>The central Norte–Sul subconcession and Porto do Açu each count once. São João da Barra is one municipality across six districts; terminals, generating units and districts add no extra identities.</p>{brazilDossiers.records.map(r=><details data-portfolio-addition={r.record_id}><summary>{r.title}</summary><p><a href={r.route}>{r.scope}</a></p><p>{r.identity_decision.rationale}</p><p><a href={r.historical_acquisition.route}>Retained acquisition record</a>. {r.historical_acquisition.decision}.</p><p>Eligible count: {r.identity_decision.eligible_count}. Dated article authored and AI self-reviewed; production verification pending.</p></details>)}</section>
  <section class="page-section"><h2>North Sea additions reviewed {northSeaDossiers.inspected_date}</h2><p>Northern Lights is one transport-and-storage project across development phases. Øygarden and Rotterdam are separate municipalities, not terminals, former municipal boundaries or whole industrial regions.</p>{northSeaDossiers.records.map(r=><details data-portfolio-addition={r.record_id}><summary>{r.title}</summary><p><a href={r.route}>{r.scope}</a></p><p>{r.identity_decision.rationale}</p><p><a href={r.historical_acquisition.route}>Retained acquisition record</a>. {r.historical_acquisition.decision}.</p><p>Eligible count: {r.identity_decision.eligible_count}. Dated article authored and AI self-reviewed; production verification pending.</p></details>)}</section>
  <section class="page-section"><h2>Stockholm additions reviewed {stockholmDossiers.inspected_date}</h2><p>The E4 bypass and Slussen redevelopment are two distinct projects. Stockholm municipality counts once; districts, tunnel sections, bridges and terminals are not additional identities.</p>{stockholmDossiers.records.map(r=><details data-portfolio-addition={r.record_id}><summary>{r.title}</summary><p><a href={r.route}>{r.scope}</a></p><p>{r.identity_decision.rationale}</p><p><a href={r.historical_acquisition.route}>Retained acquisition record</a>. {r.historical_acquisition.decision}.</p><p>Eligible count: {r.identity_decision.eligible_count}. Dated article authored and AI self-reviewed; production verification pending.</p></details>)}</section>
  <section class="page-section"><h2>Auckland additions reviewed {aucklandDossiers.inspected_date}</h2><p>City Rail Link and Central Interceptor are two distinct projects, not whole regional networks. The Auckland Council area counts as one place; stations, local boards and catchment connections are not extra identities.</p>{aucklandDossiers.records.map(r=><details data-portfolio-addition={r.record_id}><summary>{r.title}</summary><p><a href={r.route}>{r.scope}</a></p><p>{r.identity_decision.rationale}</p><p><a href={r.historical_acquisition.route}>Retained acquisition record</a>. {r.historical_acquisition.decision}.</p><p>Eligible count: {r.identity_decision.eligible_count}. Dated article authored and AI self-reviewed; production verification pending.</p></details>)}</section>
  <section class="page-section"><h2>Singapore West additions reviewed {tuasDossiers.inspected_date}</h2><p>Tuas Port and Tuas Nexus each count once across their components. The URA West Region is one subnational planning place, not a municipality or the whole country; berths, treatment modules and districts add no extra identities.</p>{tuasDossiers.records.map(r=><details data-portfolio-addition={r.record_id}><summary>{r.title}</summary><p><a href={r.route}>{r.scope}</a></p><p>{r.identity_decision.rationale}</p><p><a href={r.historical_acquisition.route}>Retained acquisition record</a>. {r.historical_acquisition.decision}.</p><p>Eligible count: {r.identity_decision.eligible_count}. Dated article authored and AI self-reviewed; production verification pending.</p></details>)}</section>
  <section class="page-section"><h2>Busan and Hamburg additions reviewed {portCitiesDossiers.inspected_date}</h2><p>Busan New Port counts once across terminals and the Busan–Changwon boundary. Busan Metropolitan City and Hamburg's municipality/city-state are two places; districts, wider regions and individual service schemes add no extra identities.</p>{portCitiesDossiers.records.map(r=><details data-portfolio-addition={r.record_id}><summary>{r.title}</summary><p><a href={r.route}>{r.scope}</a></p><p>{r.identity_decision.rationale}</p><p><a href={r.historical_acquisition.route}>Retained acquisition record</a>. {r.historical_acquisition.decision}.</p><p>Eligible count: {r.identity_decision.eligible_count}. Dated article authored and AI self-reviewed; production verification pending.</p></details>)}</section>
  <section class="page-section"><h2>Madrid and Mexico City additions reviewed {urbanServicesDossiers.inspected_date}</h2><p>Madrid Nuevo Norte counts once across its planning areas. Madrid municipality and Ciudad de México are two administrative places; regional service footprints and their districts do not add identities. Indexed-text retrieval limits are displayed.</p>{urbanServicesDossiers.records.map(r=><details data-portfolio-addition={r.record_id}><summary>{r.title}</summary><p><a href={r.route}>{r.scope}</a></p><p>{r.identity_decision.rationale}</p><p><a href={r.historical_acquisition.route}>Retained acquisition record</a>. {r.historical_acquisition.decision}.</p><p>Eligible count: {r.identity_decision.eligible_count}. Dated article authored and AI self-reviewed; production verification pending.</p></details>)}</section>
  <section class="page-section"><h2>Nordic-city additions reviewed {nordicCitiesDossiers.inspected_date}</h2><p>M3 Cityringen counts once. Copenhagen and Helsinki are new municipal identities; regional provider territories do not add places or overwrite earlier acquisition dockets.</p>{nordicCitiesDossiers.records.map(r=><details data-portfolio-addition={r.record_id}><summary>{r.title}</summary><p><a href={r.route}>{r.scope}</a></p><p>{r.identity_decision.rationale}</p>{r.historical_acquisition?<p><a href={r.historical_acquisition.route}>Retained acquisition record</a>. {r.historical_acquisition.decision}.</p>:<p>New municipal identity with no reused historical acquisition docket.</p>}<p>Eligible count: {r.identity_decision.eligible_count}. Dated article authored and AI self-reviewed; production verification pending.</p></details>)}</section>
  <section class="page-section"><h2>Swiss rail and city additions reviewed {swissRailCityDossiers.inspected_date}</h2><p>Gotthard and Ceneri are two distinct tunnel projects within a wider programme, not aliases or separately counted tubes. Zürich is one municipality, not a canton or regional utility territory. No historical acquisition docket is reused.</p>{swissRailCityDossiers.records.map(r=><details data-portfolio-addition={r.record_id}><summary>{r.title}</summary><p><a href={r.route}>{r.scope}</a></p><p>{r.identity_decision.rationale}</p><p>Eligible count: {r.identity_decision.eligible_count}. Dated article authored and AI self-reviewed; production verification pending.</p></details>)}</section>
  <section class="page-section"><h2>Kenyan corridor additions reviewed {kenyaCorridorDossiers.inspected_date}</h2><p>Mombasa–Nairobi is one railway phase, distinct from its extensions and receiving facilities. Nairobi and Mombasa are two counties, not wider commuting or commercial catchments. No historical acquisition docket is reused.</p>{kenyaCorridorDossiers.records.map(r=><details data-portfolio-addition={r.record_id}><summary>{r.title}</summary><p><a href={r.route}>{r.scope}</a></p><p>{r.identity_decision.rationale}</p><p>Eligible count: {r.identity_decision.eligible_count}. Dated article authored and AI self-reviewed; production verification pending.</p></details>)}</section>
  <section class="page-section"><h2>Gauteng railway and municipal additions reviewed {gautengMetroDossiers.inspected_date}</h2><p>Gautrain is one connected railway, not several opening stages. Johannesburg and Tshwane are separate municipalities, not the wider Gauteng or utility catchments. No historical acquisition docket is reused.</p>{gautengMetroDossiers.records.map(r=><details data-portfolio-addition={r.record_id}><summary>{r.title}</summary><p><a href={r.route}>{r.scope}</a></p><p>{r.identity_decision.rationale}</p><p>Eligible count: {r.identity_decision.eligible_count}. Dated article authored and AI self-reviewed; production verification pending.</p></details>)}</section>
  <section class="page-section"><h2>Malaysian railway and municipal additions reviewed {malaysiaMetroDossiers.inspected_date}</h2><p>The Putrajaya Line is one regional railway across its opening stages. Kuala Lumpur and Putrajaya are two distinct Federal Territories, not the entire metropolitan region or twenty precincts. No historical acquisition docket is reused.</p>{malaysiaMetroDossiers.records.map(r=><details data-portfolio-addition={r.record_id}><summary>{r.title}</summary><p><a href={r.route}>{r.scope}</a></p><p>{r.identity_decision.rationale}</p><p>Eligible count: {r.identity_decision.eligible_count}. Dated article authored and AI self-reviewed; production verification pending.</p></details>)}</section>
  <section class="page-section"><h2>Colombian railway and capital-district additions reviewed {colombiaRailDossiers.inspected_date}</h2><p>Bogotá Line 1 and Medellín’s original A/B railway are two distinct projects. Bogotá is one capital-district place, not its surrounding survey municipalities or utility service area. No historical acquisition docket is reused.</p>{colombiaRailDossiers.records.map(r=><details data-portfolio-addition={r.record_id}><summary>{r.title}</summary><p><a href={r.route}>{r.scope}</a></p><p>{r.identity_decision.rationale}</p><p>Eligible count: {r.identity_decision.eligible_count}. Dated article authored and AI self-reviewed; production verification pending.</p></details>)}</section>
  <section class="page-section"><h2>Moroccan corridor and commune additions reviewed {moroccoCorridorDossiers.inspected_date}</h2><p>The original Al Boraq corridor counts once. Tangier and Casablanca are two commune-level places, not their surrounding prefecture, region or service catchments. No historical acquisition docket is reused.</p>{moroccoCorridorDossiers.records.map(r=><details data-portfolio-addition={r.record_id}><summary>{r.title}</summary><p><a href={r.route}>{r.scope}</a></p><p>{r.identity_decision.rationale}</p><p>Eligible count: {r.identity_decision.eligible_count}. Dated article authored and AI self-reviewed; production verification pending.</p></details>)}</section>
  <section class="page-section"><h2>Portuguese water and city additions reviewed {portugalWaterCitiesDossiers.inspected_date}</h2><p>Alqueva counts as one connected scheme. Lisbon and Porto are two municipal places, not their parishes or wider service regions. Their cross-links are comparisons, not an asserted Alqueva supply connection. No historical acquisition docket is reused.</p>{portugalWaterCitiesDossiers.records.map(r=><details data-portfolio-addition={r.record_id}><summary>{r.title}</summary><p><a href={r.route}>{r.scope}</a></p><p>{r.identity_decision.rationale}</p><p>Eligible count: {r.identity_decision.eligible_count}. Dated article authored and AI self-reviewed; production verification pending.</p></details>)}</section>
  <section class="page-section"><h2>Italian rail and lagoon additions reviewed {italyRailLagoonDossiers.inspected_date}</h2><p>MOSE and Milan M4 are two distinct projects; their barriers, gates and stations are not extra identities. Venice is one municipality across six municipalità, not the entire lagoon or metropolitan city. No historical acquisition docket is reused.</p>{italyRailLagoonDossiers.records.map(r=><details data-portfolio-addition={r.record_id}><summary>{r.title}</summary><p><a href={r.route}>{r.scope}</a></p><p>{r.identity_decision.rationale}</p><p>Eligible count: {r.identity_decision.eligible_count}. Dated article authored and AI self-reviewed; production verification pending.</p></details>)}</section>
  <section class="page-section"><h2>Austrian housing and municipal additions reviewed {austriaHousingCitiesDossiers.inspected_date}</h2><p>Seestadt Aspern is one phased development programme; Vienna and Graz are two municipal places. Housing plots and service assets are not additional identities, and regional utility catchments do not expand municipal boundaries. No historical acquisition docket is reused.</p>{austriaHousingCitiesDossiers.records.map(r=><details data-portfolio-addition={r.record_id}><summary>{r.title}</summary><p><a href={r.route}>{r.scope}</a></p><p>{r.identity_decision.rationale}</p><p>Eligible count: {r.identity_decision.eligible_count}. Dated article authored and AI self-reviewed; production verification pending.</p></details>)}</section>
  <section class="page-section"><h2>Ruhr water and municipal additions reviewed {ruhrWaterCityDossiers.inspected_date}</h2><p>The Emscher sewer and PHOENIX See are two bounded projects; Dortmund is one municipality. Pumping stations and lake paths are components, not additional identities. Neither project counts the whole regional restoration umbrella, and statistical subdistricts are not additional places. No historical acquisition docket is reused.</p>{ruhrWaterCityDossiers.records.map(r=><details data-portfolio-addition={r.record_id}><summary>{r.title}</summary><p><a href={r.route}>{r.scope}</a></p><p>{r.identity_decision.rationale}</p><p>Eligible count: {r.identity_decision.eligible_count}. Dated article authored and AI self-reviewed; production verification pending.</p></details>)}</section>
  <section class="page-section"><h2>Korean energy and municipal additions reviewed {koreaEnergyCitiesDossiers.inspected_date}</h2><p>Sihwa is one named tidal plant; Seoul and Incheon are two defined municipalities. Turbines, districts, service areas and programme allocations do not add identities. The wider capital region and reclamation programme are outside these counted boundaries. No historical acquisition docket is reused.</p>{koreaEnergyCitiesDossiers.records.map(r=><details data-portfolio-addition={r.record_id}><summary>{r.title}</summary><p><a href={r.route}>{r.scope}</a></p><p>{r.identity_decision.rationale}</p><p>Eligible count: {r.identity_decision.eligible_count}. Dated article authored and AI self-reviewed; production verification pending.</p></details>)}</section>
  <section class="page-section"><h2>Istanbul crossings and municipal additions reviewed {istanbulCrossingsDossiers.inspected_date}</h2><p>Marmaray and Eurasia Tunnel are distinct rail and road projects; Istanbul is one metropolitan municipality. Stations, decks, districts and service examples do not add identities. Marmaray's Gebze end remains outside the municipal place boundary. No historical acquisition docket is reused.</p>{istanbulCrossingsDossiers.records.map(r=><details data-portfolio-addition={r.record_id}><summary>{r.title}</summary><p><a href={r.route}>{r.scope}</a></p><p>{r.identity_decision.rationale}</p><p>Eligible count: {r.identity_decision.eligible_count}. Dated article authored and AI self-reviewed; production verification pending.</p></details>)}</section>
  <section class="page-section"><h2>Finnish metro and municipal additions reviewed {finlandMetroCitiesDossiers.inspected_date}</h2><p>West Metro is one project across two delivery phases. Espoo and Tampere are separate municipalities; Helsinki retains its existing identity without recounting. Stations, company properties, district proposals and regional service catchments do not add identities. No historical acquisition docket is reused.</p>{finlandMetroCitiesDossiers.records.map(r=><details data-portfolio-addition={r.record_id}><summary>{r.title}</summary><p><a href={r.route}>{r.scope}</a></p><p>{r.identity_decision.rationale}</p><p>Eligible count: {r.identity_decision.eligible_count}. Dated article authored and AI self-reviewed; production verification pending.</p></details>)}</section>
  <section class="page-section"><h2>Andean metro and municipal additions reviewed {andesMetroCityDossiers.inspected_date}</h2><p>Quito Metro and Lima–Callao Line 2 with its contracted Line 4 branch count as two projects. Quito's metropolitan district counts once as a place. Stations, delivery stages, proposed extensions and municipal service examples do not add identities. No historical acquisition docket is reused.</p>{andesMetroCityDossiers.records.map(r=><details data-portfolio-addition={r.record_id}><summary>{r.title}</summary><p><a href={r.route}>{r.scope}</a></p><p>{r.identity_decision.rationale}</p><p>Eligible count: {r.identity_decision.eligible_count}. Dated article authored and AI self-reviewed; production verification pending.</p></details>)}</section>
  <section class="page-section"><h2>Czech railway and municipal additions reviewed {czechMetroCitiesDossiers.inspected_date}</h2><p>Prague Metro D is one project across its defined stages. Prague and Brno are two municipalities, not their wider transit, utility or river catchments. Stations, districts and component works do not add identities. No historical acquisition docket is reused.</p>{czechMetroCitiesDossiers.records.map(r=><details data-portfolio-addition={r.record_id}><summary>{r.title}</summary><p><a href={r.route}>{r.scope}</a></p><p>{r.identity_decision.rationale}</p><p>Eligible count: {r.identity_decision.eligible_count}. Dated article authored and AI self-reviewed; production verification pending.</p></details>)}</section>
  <section class="page-section"><h2>Indonesian railway and municipal additions reviewed {indonesiaRailCityDossiers.inspected_date}</h2><p>The North–South MRT and Whoosh are two named railways. Kota Bandung is one municipality, not its metropolitan region or external utility catchments. Phases, stations, feeders and utility examples do not add identities. No historical acquisition docket is reused.</p>{indonesiaRailCityDossiers.records.map(r=><details data-portfolio-addition={r.record_id}><summary>{r.title}</summary><p><a href={r.route}>{r.scope}</a></p><p>{r.identity_decision.rationale}</p><p>Eligible count: {r.identity_decision.eligible_count}. Dated article authored and AI self-reviewed; production verification pending.</p></details>)}</section>
  <section class="page-section"><h2>Senegal project and regional additions reviewed {senegalMobilityEnergyDossiers.inspected_date}</h2><p>Dakar BRT and Taïba N’Diaye are two distinct projects; the Dakar administrative region is one place. Service patterns, turbines, departments and program examples do not create extra identities. Thiès remains outside the counted region. No historical acquisition docket is reused.</p>{senegalMobilityEnergyDossiers.records.map(r=><details data-portfolio-addition={r.record_id}><summary>{r.title}</summary><p><a href={r.route}>{r.scope}</a></p><p>{r.identity_decision.rationale}</p><p>Eligible count: {r.identity_decision.eligible_count}. Dated article authored and AI self-reviewed; production verification pending.</p></details>)}</section>
  <section class="page-section"><h2>Kigali place addition reviewed {kigaliCityDossiers.inspected_date}</h2><p>Kigali is one city covering Gasabo, Kicukiro and Nyarugenge. Districts and service examples do not create extra identities; external water dependencies do not enlarge the city boundary. No historical acquisition docket is reused. Reaching the identity targets does not certify every older account as content-complete.</p>{kigaliCityDossiers.records.map(r=><details data-portfolio-addition={r.record_id}><summary>{r.title}</summary><p><a href={r.route}>{r.scope}</a></p><p>{r.identity_decision.rationale}</p><p>Eligible count: {r.identity_decision.eligible_count}. Dated article authored and AI self-reviewed; production verification pending.</p></details>)}</section>
